codex
The fresh negative gates behaved correctly. Changing the postcondition to `F` reached `floatMod(F, 1.0)` and failed on the unmet equality; changing the executed closure body to `% 2.0` reached `floatMod(F, 2.0)` and likewise failed. Both were genuine stuck obligations (exit 1), while the wrapper exited 0 only after confirming both expected failures. I’m consolidating the trust ledger and final seven-stage review now.
apply patch
